# Emoji held on the user's message while the agent works (Slack only).
# Leave commented out for the default: hourglass_flowing_sand, a built-in
# emoji present in every workspace, so a fresh install shows a correct static
# indicator with no setup.
#
#   <name>  used verbatim. For a live spinner rather than a static glyph,
#           upload a <=128 KB, 128x128 animated GIF to the workspace as a
#           custom emoji and put its name here — it animates inside the
#           reaction pill at no extra API cost.
#   (empty) SLACK_TYPING_EMOJI= turns the indicator off: no reaction and no
#           placeholder is ever posted, and Slack reverts to the same
#           (invisible) native typing call every other channel makes. This is
#           the kill switch — it needs a host restart, not a redeploy.
#
# SLACK_TYPING_EMOJI=
